   "file": "projects.md",
   "heading": "Week 1 Project: Ground Truth News Classification Evaluation",
   "text": "Week 1 Project: Ground Truth News Classification Evaluation. I manually labelled 30 news headlines across World, Sports, Business and Sci/Tech categories, then evaluated AI-generated classifications against benchmark labels using agreement rates, Cohen's Kappa, confusion matrices and model evaluation techniques. I also compared prompt-engineered AI classification against a TF-IDF machine learning model and investigated the impact of data leakage on model performance.\n\nResults: Labelled 30 news articles Achieved 83.3% agreement (25/30) between AI classifications and benchmark labels Achieved Cohen's Kappa score of 0.777 Identified Business and Sci/Tech as the most commonly confused categories Evaluated a TF-IDF model with 86.5% held-out accuracy on a larger dataset",
