   "file": "projects.md",
   "heading": "Week 2 project: Newsroom Triage app",
   "text": "Week 2 project: Newsroom Triage app. Built a Python-based news classification application using FastAPI, Gradio, and Neon Postgres. The application classifies headlines into four categories, stores results in a database, provides confidence scores, exposes API endpoints, and evaluates performance against previously labelled data. The system was split into separate frontend and backend services communicating over HTTP.\n\nResults: Built 4 API endpoints: /classify, /runs, /score and /health Migrated application data from SQLite to Neon Postgres Evaluated the system against 30 labelled headlines Baseline performance: 7/30 correct predictions, 23.3% accuracy, 0.1825 Cohen's Kappa Discovered and fixed a scoring bug where invalid predictions were incorrectly excluded from Kappa calculations",
